  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity Building to crack down on Tiger Poaching and Trade in Bhutan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to build Forest Protection and Surveillance Unit (FPSU) trainer capacity in law enforcement monitoring tools, intelligence tools and standard anti-poaching ranger trainings as per the IUCN standards for national roll out. The project will support capacity building of FPSU and divisional field staff to train others on SMART and standard anti-poaching ranger training, as well as to best utilize the Bhutan Forestry Enforcement Database (BhuFED), and integrate SMART with BhuFED as well as increase national awareness on law enforcement tools and trainings available in Bhutan through FPSU.</narrative>
  </description>
